-- Native module algebra and degree-zero/degree-one gluing (Serre note §3).
-- Reviewed fraction, numerator and power interfaces are followed by actual
-- module structures over A_f, finite matrix/cube clearing and powered
-- partitions. Both gluing theorems use the actual basic restriction maps.
-- Cochain, family, structural module and ring carriers remain transparent;
-- equality and composition use their named equations. Quotient aliases in
-- gluing comparisons identify these carriers, without reopening quotient,
-- function-extensionality, fraction or ring-localisation proof constructions.
